+---
+
+## Incremental Markdown parser write recovery
+
+`tests/test_smd_parser_write_recovery.py` runs the actual `_smdNewParser()`, `_smdWrite()` and `_smdEndParser()` functions from `static/messages.js` against the bundled streaming Markdown parser through Node. It needs no npm dependencies, application server, session or provider.
+
+```bash
+./scripts/test.sh tests/test_smd_parser_write_recovery.py -q
+```
+
+The regression injects one write exception before input is consumed and one after the parser consumes a partial fragment. On the next full display snapshot, the renderer must rebuild the failed parser and retain the complete word prefix; a normal incremental write and terminal parser flush must remain intact. The state under test is the parser display cache and its last successful written snapshot. It does not change `INFLIGHT`, the canonical session or transcript semantics, and an injected display exception is not evidence of saved-report corruption.
+
+For manual fixture review, compare the transient display after the next snapshot separately from the final canonical message. A completed canonical message can repair the baseline display even when the earlier live prefix was missing.
 
